Z||000000||drednot||03-26-2001||08:03 PM||||Ok, Here is the question--  I have just found a 1988 Fiero GT for sale.  The interior is perfect, has t-tops, wing, all the options, good sail panels, non-scratched windows etc etc.  The thing only has 24,000 miles on it.  Only problem is it has been in a wreck.  The 2 front fenders are scratched up, one has a big crack.  The front and rear bumpers are dented in (not that bad).  The one thing that I am concerned about, is that it has a bent control arm.  The front wheel is visibly tilted outward.  Other than that it is almost perfect.  What do you guys think??  is it worth $500 bucks?  how hard would this be to fix?  Thanks for the info.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Hank is Here||03-26-2001||08:06 PM||||Well, I think I can speak for all  (if not most) here.  Go for it!!! Sounds like a deal and a half.  If you decide not to do it however would you mind emailing me the info on hte car.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Hank is Here<BR>87 GT<BR>88 Coupe<BR>84 SE<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://a1060.g.akamai.net/f/1060/597/30minutes/www.zing.com/picture/p60e80970138058d8e3fae31692e151e0/fef43e85.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||03-26-2001||08:24 PM||||Yes, definately worth every penny!!!||||reg||14
Z||000003||GoCartGuy||03-27-2001||02:29 AM||||If you don't buy it I will.  I've been wanting a T-Top and $500 is well worth it.  If you have any experience with minor body work you can do most of the fixes yourself.  And the bent arm won't be too expensive to fix, I paid quite a good deal more for mine.  I'm jealous you  found such a steal.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
